def length_of_longest_substring(s: str) -> int:
    char_index_map = {}
    start = 0
    max_length = 0

    for end, char in enumerate(s):
        if char in char_index_map and char_index_map[char] >= start:
            start = char_index_map[char] + 1
        else:
            max_length = max(max_length, end - start + 1)

        char_index_map[char] = end

    return max_length
```

This function uses a sliding window approach to keep track of the longest substring without repeating characters. It maintains a dictionary to map characters to their most recent index and updates the start of the window whenever a duplicate character is found. The time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the string, and the space complexity is O(min(m, n)), where m is the size of the character set.
